Today we had our second DCM (district counsel meeting) and it didn=E2=80=99=
t
exactly go well to say the least. Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 was trying to g=
o somewhere and
kept losing his train of thought to the point where he cancelled DCM
halfway through and we postponed it until the next day. It was a bit yikes
for sure. Anyways I gave him some time to think about what happened, where
he had wanted to go, and to pray about things. He thought about it for an
hour or two, and we went out to go and get lunch. We ended up going to
Mcdonalds because I was missing it after not having it since Marugame, so
we biked around 15-20 minutes to get there. It was fun, but I def had too
many fries lol. After eating, WE WERE ABLE TO DO SOME FINDING! We went and
did housing for probably 2 or more hours near the Mcdonalds, and it was
awesome. We didn't have any super meaningful interactions or anything from
it but it felt so nice to go out and do something. On the way back to our
bikes, we passed by a group of teenage boys hanging out under a bridge. I
said =E2=80=9CHello,=E2=80=9D and when they responded with a very Japanese =
=E2=80=9CHello=E2=80=9D I told
them that their English was really good (in Japanese). A few of them
laughed and as we walked away they whispered about how handsome I was,
proud guy moment there. Pretty much this whole day after eating Mcdonalds
my head was buzzing from the heat, and it was a pretty miserable headache
back at the apartment. Great day!

Weird silly awkward story sort of, one of our friend Habir who we were
helping with Jkaiwa decided to drop us. The way it went down is we were
going through our list of referrals, and saw one that we hadn't heard from
in a while. Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 sent them a text message asking if th=
ey were still
interested in meeting up with us sometime for Jkaiwa, if they had any
interest in that sort of thing. Anyways it turns out that it was that same
friend, we just didn't realize they had another name/number in our area
book. Super awkward, he told us he didn't want to meet anymore with
Christian missionaries. When we gave him good wishes though, he told us
thanks and said he'd be down to meet up if we are ever near his hometown.
So I guess we aren=E2=80=99t exactly on the worst terms or anything which i=
s great.

Today we had the real DCM for real this time, and it was much more of a
success. I think that maybe Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 just needed a bit mor=
e time to think
about what he wanted to achieve with it, and it worked out in the end.
Eikaiwa this =EF=BD=97eek was super silly, there was one guy (pretty appare=
nt
smoker) in there who was making silly comments the whole time, but not to
the point where he was ever a nuisance. Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 also brou=
ght up the word
=E2=80=9CCrush=E2=80=9D and spent ages explaining it because it's very comp=
licated
grammar-wise. The one goofy man from before kept on asking questions about
it too, it was so funny. He says he is going to say it to a Japanese girl
because they aren=E2=80=99t going to understand what he means lol.

We got to have dinner at the Bishops house AGAIN. It was awesome, we got to
do another roleplay lesson to practice our teaching skills. I think it went
over pretty well considering how bad it usually is when me and my comp try
teaching together =F0=9F=98=85=F0=9F=98=82 I think we still have yet to rea=
lly sit down and
tell each other what we are trying to do when we teach, bit messy. Anyways,
it was really good this time around. After that, we proceeded to eat. And
eat. And eat. I ate literally everything that was placed in front of me,
and we thought we were safe. Except we hadn=E2=80=99t eaten desert, I knew =
there
was no reason to be hopeful=E2=80=A6 The bishop=E2=80=99s wife came out of =
the kitchen with
two huge slices of cake and ice cream. I ate it all. But, it was time for
us to go, and I had to stand up and walk home in the rain. Standing up. Oh
that was not good. As we left the front of the house and walked down the
stairs to the road the title wave came. I launched that dinner at the
bishops house 5 feet in front of me down the gutter on the hill. It was
wild, I felt like I was in a movie. It was awesome. Fortunately neither my
companion or the Bishop and his wife saw anything. I told my companion
about it afterwards and he said he was glad cause if he saw me throw up he
would have too =F0=9F=98=82 The rain probably washed any bit of evidence aw=
ay as
well, so that was definitely a blessing. I am counting on you, my email
readers, not to inform the Osako family of this incident lol.

On Friday we went out again to go and eat with Jiro. This time he drove us
in the car, freaked out about us knowing a lot of Japanese music, and we
arrived safely at a Chinese restaurant. It was amazing, but my mouth is
always torn up after eating fried chicken. Raw for the rest of the day,
oof. Anyways we practiced a bit of English with him while we were at the
restaurant, because of his huge desire to be a pro at speaking. While we
ate I accidentally spilled some water, and I said =E2=80=9Coops=E2=80=9D. H=
e repeated it
back to me while motioning across his chest, definitely thinking I had said
=E2=80=9Cboobs.=E2=80=9D It was hard to maintain my composure but I helped =
him clear up the
difference in pronunciation for the two words. I also made sure to tell him
he shouldn=E2=80=99t really have a reason to use the word a lot lol. Also o=
n the
drive home I discovered that he has the exact same bluetooth car adapter as
I do. Same =E2=80=9Cbluetooth pairing=E2=80=9D voice as my minivan back at =
home. Legendary.

Saturday morning we had a Zoom Eikaiwa class with a member of a nearby ward
named Aime. I think she is probably a less active member, and she was
referred to us to teach from some other elders. It was super fun, and she's
like super good at English. She is finding out which of 7 restaurants she
is assigned to at a hotel, and when asked which one she wants to work at,
she said the bar, because she wants to learn more about alcohol =F0=9F=92=
=80
Hopefully we can keep being a positive influence for her!

This week we also had a big surprise. There is an emergency transfer, and
my comp from 2 transfers ago, Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 is going to be in a =
trio with me and
Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 for the last 2 weeks of the transfer =F0=9F=98=82=
=F0=9F=98=82 Can=E2=80=99t escape him =F0=9F=98=9C It
is Pday as I am typing this and we just picked him up today. I am hoping
that he can help jumpstart our companionship. For the last week most of our
day has been spent at the church. I have been trying to make the most of
the time i.e. writing notes on the back of cards to give away to people we
house/street and reading from the Book of Mormon and the Saints series
(still on book 1 lol). I could probably do more to motivate my companion
but I have been feeling pretty unenthusiastic about it sadly. I regret that
I didn=E2=80=99t make us go out and do more things. I hope you can tell fro=
m this
email that things are slowly getting better though, I think. With a solo
Zone leader Mackay=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 to add to our companionship maybe we c=
an do a better
job of holding each other accountable for things. I don=E2=80=99t think tha=
t this
last week was as much of a waste of time as it has been in the past though,
which is really good. Focus on the progress!

Today I have some gospel focused art that I have made that I would love to
share! This is the tree of life, spoken about in 1st Nephi. I have had some
meaningful time thinking about what the symbols are in these chapters of
the Book of Mormon. It was really fun to make this art, and I hope I can
keep the same energy throughout the rest of my mission=E2=80=99s art creati=
on.






I love all of you so much. I am not a perfect person, not even a perfect
missionary! I know that as I turn to the Lord for strength I will be able
to do more than I would be able to on my own, which is a reassurance. I
would highly encourage each of you to do the same! I wish you the best
throughout this next week, I hope that you can wish me the best as well! I
will try to get out more responses and emails to people. It's tough to
balance the time. This is a special time in my life, and I am probably not
gonna have a chance to do something quite like this again. I will try and
live it to the best of my ability.

--00000000000025bda60631a320a2
